{"cases": [{"case_id": "sha256:065848a4510703cc9867a12d4c08e14ba14fa670207222ac9af062c6d7e18a26", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1082", "family": "ifeval-source-1082", "sample_id": "sha256:c0ca4c0163169259e64e4d91ac68a02e4faac660c4b2ea7e26cf2e963a3587c7", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a story of exactly 2 paragraphs about a man who wakes up one day and realizes that he's inside a video game. Separate the paragraphs with the markdown divider: ***", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Elias woke to the sound of cheerful music and a glowing message hovering above his bed: **QUEST STARTED: ESCAPE THE TOWER**. His room looked familiar, but everything shimmered at the edges, as if painted with squares of light. When he reached for the door, a red bar appeared over his wrist labeled HEALTH, and a tiny golden coin dropped from his pocket. Outside, the neighborhood stretched beneath a sky filled with floating icons, while strangers repeated the same three sentences whenever he passed.\\n\\nAt the town square, a hooded child handed Elias a wooden sword and pointed toward the distant castle. \\u201cThe final boss is waiting,\\u201d she said, her voice echoing like a recording. Elias looked at the sword, then at the impossible world around him, and understood that every fear he had ever avoided had been turned into a level. He tightened his grip, stepped onto the glowing path, and smiled when the words **PLAYER ONE READY** appeared above the horizon.\\n***\", \"checks\": {\"0:length_constraints:number_paragraphs\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1082"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:1ff0b2cfce147f800be6350b008917c10b8baeb6a0fed862573ceed271ecae1a", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2716", "family": "ifeval-source-2716", "sample_id": "sha256:ff144ac3dbf2b246c34b68563e8c322fdf25297017c57a6656fd4688ad414088", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a cover letter for a job in a tech company. Make sure to use the word \"the\" once or less.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Dear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI am excited to apply for a role at your tech company. With experience in problem-solving, collaboration, and building practical digital solutions, I am eager to contribute to a team focused on innovation and meaningful results.\\n\\nMy background has strengthened my ability to learn quickly, manage priorities, communicate clearly, and turn complex challenges into effective solutions. I enjoy working across teams, taking ownership, and continuously improving both products and processes.\\n\\nI would welcome an opportunity to bring my skills, curiosity, and enthusiasm to your organization. Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to discussing how I can contribute to your team.\\n\\nSincerely,  \\n[Your Name]\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2716"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:228d4f48df3b04fd12514ee7e89b70503eee9fbc604173c53443701ebe1e71cf", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3109", "family": "ifeval-source-3109", "sample_id": "sha256:16906ea1965d75bef0a41e7042261021e39122bdc1bc323159179d22e3372068", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a short fiction about adulthood. Make sure the word cousins appears more than 2 times.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"At thirty, Mara inherited her grandmother\\u2019s old house and discovered that adulthood was mostly deciding what to keep.\\n\\nHer cousins arrived with boxes, memories, and strong opinions. The cousins argued over dishes, photographs, and who had loved Grandma best. By sunset, even the youngest cousins were laughing in the dusty kitchen.\\n\\nMara kept the yellow teapot. She sold the house, paid her bills, and planted a tree in her apartment courtyard. Adulthood, she realized, was not knowing everything\\u2014it was choosing what mattered, then making room for it to grow.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-3109"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:48b7a65e7d28f10e803d0d6d1544a7e5c30c9c10d94974ed7d2cd6df1b47a27d", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-201", "family": "ifeval-source-201", "sample_id": "sha256:772de99196c6b3605732198cfc2b8c1a1026b9b79386e411ae00938528634987", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a story from a perspective of a man. Include some conversation in the story. Avoid using the letter i more than twice.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"At dawn, a man named Tom woke to a soft knock.\\n\\n\\u201cTom, are you up?\\u201d called Mara.\\n\\n\\u201cYes,\\u201d he said. \\u201cCome on in.\\u201d\\n\\nMara held a small box. \\u201cThis was left at your door.\\u201d\\n\\nTom took it and saw no mark, no note, no clue. He slid the lid back. A warm gold glow rose from within.\\n\\n\\u201cWhat does it do?\\u201d Mara asked.\\n\\nTom held the box near the wall. A door of light took shape.\\n\\n\\u201cWant to see what lies past it?\\u201d he asked.\\n\\nMara took his hand. \\u201cYes. Let\\u2019s go.\\u201d\\n\\nTom stepped through, glad that dawn had brought more than a new day.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:letter_frequency\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-201"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:b3c38ea6d954a9d024cb8e0d95bd4aa54860644e3e05cfa28143fdf5cb8a47bc", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2662", "family": "ifeval-source-2662", "sample_id": "sha256:000244280afd8b88daced8113b634ad3cd6e88fcf2bae273605e007a4e92aaf0", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a tweet for the president of the United States. The tweet should include the keywords \"engages\" and \"lightly\".", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"America engages with the world from a position of strength\\u2014and we will act lightly when diplomacy can deliver results. Together, we\\u2019re building a safer, stronger future. \\ud83c\\uddfa\\ud83c\\uddf8\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:existence\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2662"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:bf19cff7973f1ad5dc0e1748c56402b10ae762f430cc739c5d65186679aa03f8", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3126", "family": "ifeval-source-3126", "sample_id": "sha256:2f06a5500aeda1f866e8290dec0116c716e17f988e19475a05f311456dfafbf9", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write an article named \"How to conduct a job interview\". Include at least one placeholder, such as [question].", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"# How to Conduct a Job Interview\\n\\nA successful job interview helps you evaluate a candidate\\u2019s skills, experience, and suitability for the role while giving them a clear understanding of your organization. Use the following steps to conduct a fair and effective interview.\\n\\n## 1. Prepare in Advance\\n\\nReview the candidate\\u2019s r\\u00e9sum\\u00e9, cover letter, and application materials before the interview. Identify areas you want to explore and prepare a consistent set of questions related to the role.\\n\\nYou may also want to define:\\n\\n- The essential skills for the position\\n- The qualities of an ideal candidate\\n- How responses will be evaluated\\n- Who will participate in the interview\\n\\n## 2. Create a Welcoming Environment\\n\\nBegin by introducing yourself and explaining the interview structure. Briefly describe the company, the position, and what the conversation will cover. A friendly opening can help the candidate feel comfortable and encourage more thoughtful responses.\\n\\n## 3. Ask Clear, Relevant Questions\\n\\nUse open-ended questions that encourage candidates to describe their experience and decision-making process. For example:\\n\\n- \\u201cTell me about a challenging project you completed.\\u201d\\n- \\u201cHow do you prioritize competing deadlines?\\u201d\\n- \\u201c[question]\\u201d\\n- \\u201cWhat interests you about this position?\\u201d\\n\\nAsk follow-up questions when you need clarification, but avoid interrupting or leading the candidate toward a particular answer.\\n\\n## 4. Evaluate Skills and Experience\\n\\nFocus on evidence of the candidate\\u2019s abilities. Ask them to provide specific examples of past work, including the situation, actions they took, and results they achieved. This approach can reveal both technical competence and practical judgment.\\n\\n## 5. Assess Cultural and Team Fit Carefully\\n\\nConsider how the candidate may collaborate, communicate, and respond to feedback. Avoid making judgments based on personality preferences or personal similarities. Evaluate only qualities that are relevant to performing the job successfully.\\n\\n## 6. Allow Time for Candidate Questions\\n\\nGive the candidate an opportunity to ask questions about the role, team, expectations, and company. Their questions may also indicate how well they have prepared and what matters to them professionally.\\n\\n## 7. Take Structured Notes\\n\\nRecord objective observations during or immediately after the interview. Use the same evaluation criteria for every candidate, and distinguish evidence from assumptions. Avoid documenting irrelevant personal information.\\n\\n## 8. Conclude Professionally\\n\\nThank the candidate for their time and explain the next steps, including the expected timeline for a decision. Be honest and respectful throughout the process, regardless of the outcome.\\n\\n## 9. Review Candidates Fairly\\n\\nAfter all interviews, compare candidates against the predefined requirements rather than relying on memory or intuition. Discuss evidence with the hiring team, document the reasoning behind the decision, and follow applicable employment laws and organizational policies.\\n\\nA well-conducted interview is structured, relevant, respectful, and consistent. It should help both the employer and the candidate determine whether the opportunity is a good match.\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_content:number_placeholders\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-3126"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:ccd7b47f73de357b162df3190f626bb445355fb75b12894305f1f50f50b8907c", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1645", "family": "ifeval-source-1645", "sample_id": "sha256:1a2c724f038ff813c292224ec2b5cc716dc7c89e591a30925957921adcb430d3", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Create a riddle about the name Sheldon using only 10 words. Make sure to only use capital letters in your entire response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"WHO AM I? A BRAINY FRIEND WITH BOWTIES, SCIENCE, KNOCKING.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_capital\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1645"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:d4bf8d58641fd2029a868f2f622fcda753c90a74e3e1d6d6f5486d0d479c6ccb", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3057", "family": "ifeval-source-3057", "sample_id": "sha256:acd6e7ca8082d88ff30fc7d6f613e92d975a8891d1858f8af2896a1dbf2b69f2", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Please write a riddle about the inverse function with a title wrapped in double angular brackets, i.e. <<title>>.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"<<The Function That Turns Back>>\\n\\nI take what you give and undo its way,  \\nReturning each answer to where inputs lay.  \\nSwap x and y, and I\\u2019m revealed\\u2014  \\nWhat one function does, I make unsealed.\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_format:title\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-3057"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": []}

