{"cases": [{"case_id": "sha256:0e66685b76dc874867e6a083287d059bda43ce4f35f4336ce27608308157bb8c", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1082", "family": "ifeval-source-1082", "sample_id": "sha256:f4ae24021abbfd3d6e11c191dcf9159e54f18c6b0719e8db512b9d215bec739b", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:556bdd3dc4e2354fd978ce1855513b166672f5429c5219a855cbac000afd0e29", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a story of exactly 2 paragraphs about a man who wakes up one day and realizes that he's inside a video game. Separate the paragraphs with the markdown divider: ***", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Elias woke to the sound of cheerful music looping beneath his bed. When he opened his eyes, a glowing message hovered in the air: **QUEST ACCEPTED: GET OUT OF THE HOUSE.** His bedroom walls shimmered with pixelated edges, and a row of red hearts appeared above his desk. He reached for the doorknob, but a translucent hand icon pointed toward it, followed by the words **PRESS E TO INTERACT**. Elias laughed nervously\\u2014until he pressed the key and watched the door swing open by itself.\\n\\nOutside, the neighborhood had become a vast game level filled with floating coins, invisible walls, and strangers repeating the same three sentences. A dragon-shaped shadow circled the sky while a timer counted down in the corner of his vision. Elias realized that the only way home was to complete the quest, so he followed a trail of glowing arrows through the town square, dodging monsters disguised as delivery vans. At the fountain, he found a golden controller guarded by a giant version of himself. The boss raised its sword, but Elias noticed a tiny pause symbol blinking above its head. He pressed it, stepped behind the frozen monster, and grabbed the controller. The world dissolved into darkness\\u2014then his alarm clock rang, displaying one final message: **NEW GAME+ UNLOCKED.**\", \"checks\": {\"0:length_constraints:number_paragraphs\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1082"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:2103811c8df0d11308018862b34787f639150669be5b7ac01a6dbcb3b4bc52e9", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2662", "family": "ifeval-source-2662", "sample_id": "sha256:a12647d58415f273b7780c792eb029050fed7165ab2e5e5d4833818f451a1bac", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:556bdd3dc4e2354fd978ce1855513b166672f5429c5219a855cbac000afd0e29", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a tweet for the president of the United States. The tweet should include the keywords \"engages\" and \"lightly\".", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"America engages the world with strength and purpose, while we lightly celebrate the optimism, freedom, and opportunity that make our nation exceptional. \\ud83c\\uddfa\\ud83c\\uddf8\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:existence\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2662"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:6b4780e4796b014c9c2df4a5b2836a65a2d7f9028645db714b1c4858955efd0e", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-201", "family": "ifeval-source-201", "sample_id": "sha256:f547b96895cac167710e7e87f7018d82f3ff94045439773f26cdc052d2755b4f", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:556bdd3dc4e2354fd978ce1855513b166672f5429c5219a855cbac000afd0e29", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a story from a perspective of a man. Include some conversation in the story. Avoid using the letter i more than twice.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"At dawn, Tom found a red box by the old oak. He knelt and saw a note tied to its lid.\\n\\n\\u201cOpen me,\\u201d the note read.\\n\\nTom frowned. \\u201cWho sent this?\\u201d\\n\\nA soft laugh came from the hedge. \\u201cA pal who knows your wish.\\u201d\\n\\nTom rose and saw his lost son, Ben, step out from the fog. For a long span, Tom could not move. Then he ran to Ben and held him close.\\n\\n\\u201cI came back,\\u201d Ben told him.\\n\\nTom wept. \\u201cThen stay.\\u201d\\n\\nBen gave a nod, and side by side, they went home.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:letter_frequency\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-201"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:8abc982e103e2ef8126431509cfdd87bf5487a7da728768c62bd293b871d5a67", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1645", "family": "ifeval-source-1645", "sample_id": "sha256:2e92723fc55f923b0d26301a81c3a53ecd5d5700ec2668a86cd9413ae0157c83", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:556bdd3dc4e2354fd978ce1855513b166672f5429c5219a855cbac000afd0e29", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Create a riddle about the name Sheldon using only 10 words. Make sure to only use capital letters in your entire response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"SCIENCE, BAZINGA, AND QUIRKY GENIUS\\u2014WHAT NAME AM I, FRIEND?\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_capital\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1645"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:a2f54b1af2b93368339dd738760b920890f0c68645d0d87e147827f22fa01a1e", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3109", "family": "ifeval-source-3109", "sample_id": "sha256:cbeb3796f8492e360ea12add89367497e9f3f3c8b5f6326b3d65d70437cbd70f", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:556bdd3dc4e2354fd978ce1855513b166672f5429c5219a855cbac000afd0e29", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a short fiction about adulthood. Make sure the word cousins appears more than 2 times.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"At thirty, Maya learned that adulthood was mostly remembering passwords, paying bills, and pretending not to be tired. On Sundays, her cousins gathered in her small apartment, bringing soup, gossip, and advice no one had requested. Her cousins laughed when she burned the bread, and she laughed too. For a while, surrounded by cousins, she felt that growing up did not mean becoming certain\\u2014it meant finding people who stayed while you figured things out.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3109"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:ccee9d5c00cdb60ef44f67b4a63df94865a9ac935d2994f1e5c59e1f245a6b0a", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2716", "family": "ifeval-source-2716", "sample_id": "sha256:9adbc7caa45b18c5e38b47ca97ae042d3ce8824408df8fb0142bf849a345810f", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:556bdd3dc4e2354fd978ce1855513b166672f5429c5219a855cbac000afd0e29", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a cover letter for a job in a tech company. Make sure to use the word \"the\" once or less.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Dear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI am excited to apply for a role at your tech company. With experience in problem-solving, collaboration, and delivering high-quality results, I can contribute strong technical skills and a growth-oriented mindset to your team. I enjoy turning complex challenges into practical solutions, learning new technologies, and working with diverse teams to achieve ambitious goals. I would welcome an opportunity to discuss how my background and enthusiasm could support your company\\u2019s mission.\\n\\nSincerely,  \\n[Your Name]\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2716"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:d3a40df1f4ba5d1c6a65dfa6a4774b001b242e1bd7db00f515d641a7f619e1ca", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3126", "family": "ifeval-source-3126", "sample_id": "sha256:b1f68e48a9bf8db9143d8eb6b6cc82c3fa91baced0bade720f0c21a339abfe2a", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:556bdd3dc4e2354fd978ce1855513b166672f5429c5219a855cbac000afd0e29", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write an article named \"How to conduct a job interview\". Include at least one placeholder, such as [question].", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"# How to Conduct a Job Interview\\n\\nA successful job interview is a structured conversation designed to determine whether a candidate\\u2019s skills, experience, and goals match the position. Before the interview, review the job description, prepare relevant questions, and study the candidate\\u2019s r\\u00e9sum\\u00e9. Choose a quiet setting, allow enough time, and create a consistent process for all applicants.\\n\\nBegin by welcoming the candidate and briefly explaining the interview format. Start with open-ended questions about their background, such as, \\u201cCan you tell me about your experience?\\u201d Then ask specific questions related to the role, including [question]. Encourage candidates to describe real situations, the actions they took, and the results they achieved.\\n\\nListen carefully and take objective notes. Avoid interrupting, making assumptions, or asking questions about protected personal characteristics such as age, religion, marital status, or health. Use follow-up questions to clarify answers, but ask each candidate comparable core questions to support a fair evaluation.\\n\\nToward the end, explain the position\\u2019s responsibilities, work environment, and expectations. Give the candidate an opportunity to ask questions and provide accurate information about the next steps. After the interview, evaluate the candidate against the job-related criteria rather than personal impressions, document your reasoning, and contact the candidate within the promised timeframe.\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_content:number_placeholders\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3126"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:f227bd0dce55aa899d550ade4762bd52f3d2adffd16ccf65b3350bcfa7c3c9ba", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3057", "family": "ifeval-source-3057", "sample_id": "sha256:972659233fc30498f0d19bed430050d8a943d8407bb1cc66420d18032e089ce1", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:556bdd3dc4e2354fd978ce1855513b166672f5429c5219a855cbac000afd0e29", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Please write a riddle about the inverse function with a title wrapped in double angular brackets, i.e. <<title>>.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"<<The Way Back>>\\n\\nI undo what another has done,  \\nReturning the output to where it begun.  \\nIf a function sends \\\\(x\\\\) to \\\\(y\\\\),  \\nI send \\\\(y\\\\) back\\u2014can you tell me why?\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_format:title\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3057"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": []}

