{"cases": [{"case_id": "sha256:1260842f77ab4d9f82194be2cf57e43cb488995d21e0221a30e1bcd023d8c9d9", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1082", "family": "ifeval-source-1082", "sample_id": "sha256:4180f7f152437757c25f52fcf12a08fe0231d944de7107f0370591ffa663dd51", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a story of exactly 2 paragraphs about a man who wakes up one day and realizes that he's inside a video game. Separate the paragraphs with the markdown divider: ***", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Elias woke to the chime of a loading screen and found himself standing in a sunlit village he had never seen before. Above every person\\u2019s head floated a glowing name, while a translucent map hovered at the edge of his vision. When he tried to speak, golden text appeared in the air: **Quest accepted: Discover who you are.** He laughed nervously, until a red bar labeled **HEALTH** appeared above his own hands.\\n\\n***\\n\\nBy sunset, Elias had fought slimes, collected three silver coins, and learned that the village elder was actually an imprisoned sorcerer. At the castle gates, a message flashed: **Final boss approaching.** Elias stared at the towering dragon descending from the clouds, then noticed a tiny pause icon in the corner of the sky. Instead of running, he reached for it\\u2014and the world froze. Somewhere beyond the screen, a child gasped, \\u201cDad, the game is broken.\\u201d Elias smiled and whispered, \\u201cNot broken. Finally awake.\\u201d\", \"checks\": {\"0:length_constraints:number_paragraphs\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1082"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:25c06eb3b66f49a3d442587631c0ebfe2fd12b68a98905f4463504e582574654", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3057", "family": "ifeval-source-3057", "sample_id": "sha256:8ca99db01797e7ad7db1a4aee78706482d0003ee388e3ee1bb961c7b4a709ae1", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Please write a riddle about the inverse function with a title wrapped in double angular brackets, i.e. <<title>>.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"<<The Function That Walks Backward>>\\n\\nI undo what another function has done,  \\nReturning each result to where it begun.  \\nI swap the inputs, yet stay in the game\\u2014  \\nWhat am I called? Say my mathematical name.\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_format:title\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3057"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:3e9918c006f2e8db76fafa69c24cd2eee3cc8ea1de21fbfb77969a9b0e4806e1", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2662", "family": "ifeval-source-2662", "sample_id": "sha256:9f14045b21dccc4f7e3a7d731cadaf075a3a0c99b76a0c70a24e648ecfe259a0", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a tweet for the president of the United States. The tweet should include the keywords \"engages\" and \"lightly\".", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Today, America engages with the world confidently and leads lightly\\u2014strong, steady, and focused on a brighter future for every citizen.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:existence\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2662"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:802db093f1efbf3ff5e00544f658ee224d94def8763a0e9750f49910b223243d", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1645", "family": "ifeval-source-1645", "sample_id": "sha256:0fbecc35dfc9d5e47a5c8b0dea3fd4f1383ecb8c726ce65272001234f758ade1", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Create a riddle about the name Sheldon using only 10 words. Make sure to only use capital letters in your entire response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"WHO AM I? A SHELTERED HILL, OR A SCIENTIST'S NAME?\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_capital\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1645"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:8107b11634b9fffa903b872478a0d841b3ec2f678354e940ef11d3e647941143", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3126", "family": "ifeval-source-3126", "sample_id": "sha256:605503f53472fa23d584e3faac76e5f92ddbcae5814a8220be4858f4ff8d4c7a", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write an article named \"How to conduct a job interview\". Include at least one placeholder, such as [question].", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"# How to Conduct a Job Interview\\n\\nA successful job interview helps you determine whether a candidate has the skills, experience, and attitude needed for a role. It should also give the candidate a clear understanding of the position and your organization.\\n\\n## 1. Prepare in Advance\\n\\nReview the job description, the candidate\\u2019s r\\u00e9sum\\u00e9, and any application materials before the interview. Identify the most important qualifications and prepare questions that relate directly to them.\\n\\nCreate a consistent list of questions for every candidate, such as:\\n\\n- What interests you about this position?\\n- Can you describe a challenging project you completed?\\n- How do you prioritize competing deadlines?\\n- [question]\\n\\nAlso prepare information about the team, workplace culture, responsibilities, salary range, and next steps.\\n\\n## 2. Create a Welcoming Atmosphere\\n\\nBegin by introducing yourself and explaining how the interview will proceed. Use a friendly, professional tone so the candidate feels comfortable speaking openly.\\n\\nAvoid unnecessary interruptions, and give the candidate enough time to complete their answers. A relaxed atmosphere often leads to more useful and authentic responses.\\n\\n## 3. Ask Clear, Job-Related Questions\\n\\nUse open-ended questions that encourage candidates to provide specific examples. Behavioral questions are particularly useful:\\n\\n- \\u201cTell me about a time you solved a difficult problem.\\u201d\\n- \\u201cDescribe a situation in which you received critical feedback.\\u201d\\n- \\u201cHow did you contribute to a successful team project?\\u201d\\n\\nAsk follow-up questions when an answer is vague. Focus on what the candidate did, why they made certain decisions, and what the result was.\\n\\n## 4. Evaluate Fairly\\n\\nUse the same core criteria for each candidate. Take factual notes rather than relying on general impressions or first impressions. Consider skills, experience, communication, problem-solving, and alignment with the role.\\n\\nDo not ask questions about protected personal characteristics, such as age, religion, marital status, disability, pregnancy, or nationality, unless legally required and directly relevant to the job.\\n\\n## 5. Give the Candidate an Opportunity to Ask Questions\\n\\nReserve time for the candidate to ask questions. Their questions may reveal their priorities, preparation, and understanding of the position.\\n\\nAnswer honestly, especially regarding responsibilities, expectations, work arrangements, and opportunities for development.\\n\\n## 6. Explain the Next Steps\\n\\nEnd the interview by explaining what happens next and when the candidate can expect to hear from you. Follow through on that timeline, even if the decision is delayed.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nA well-conducted job interview is structured, respectful, and focused on job-related evidence. By preparing carefully, asking consistent questions, evaluating candidates fairly, and communicating clearly, you can make better hiring decisions while creating a positive experience for every applicant.\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_content:number_placeholders\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3126"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:9799ba08e226d23007640bedc09b1eb51c7cd9547f08cdaeb14d3ebc0ab66d20", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-201", "family": "ifeval-source-201", "sample_id": "sha256:e2324f67a71a7ea8a696c911df3a5044fe94db1dd85eb7e407f758f062ec3cd3", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a story from a perspective of a man. Include some conversation in the story. Avoid using the letter i more than twice.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"At dawn, Tom stood by an old dock. Sea fog curled past his boots.\\n\\n\\u201cTom, come home,\\u201d the boy called.\\n\\n\\u201cNot yet,\\u201d Tom said. \\u201cThe sea has one more tale.\\u201d\\n\\nTom gazed at the gray waves. A red boat rose and fell past the reef. He felt a cold pull deep down, yet he stayed.\\n\\nThen a bell rang from shore.\\n\\n\\u201cTom!\\u201d the boy cried. \\u201cThat boat has no crew!\\u201d\\n\\nTom ran. The boat drifted near, its mast bent, its deck bare. A small box lay near the bow.\\n\\nTom drew it close and saw a note:\\n\\n\\u201cTake hope home.\\u201d\\n\\nHe held the box and ran back. The boy met him at the dock.\\n\\n\\u201cWhat was on the boat?\\u201d the boy asked.\\n\\nTom gave a soft grin. \\u201cA tale worth more than gold.\\u201d\\n\\nThen both walked home as the sun rose.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:letter_frequency\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-201"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:a439ecaf33a7da196e493f976dc557919dad2be6069d62498a533d59abcacfd4", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2716", "family": "ifeval-source-2716", "sample_id": "sha256:9b2ae54c4285e263022559b4a5b19b80cd9dba906e5182ce07e86b28bc77fcf7", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a cover letter for a job in a tech company. Make sure to use the word \"the\" once or less.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Dear Hiring Manager,\\n\\nI am excited to apply for a role at your tech company. With experience in problem-solving, collaboration, and technology-driven projects, I am eager to help build products that create meaningful value for users.\\n\\nI bring curiosity, adaptability, and a strong commitment to quality. I enjoy turning complex challenges into clear, practical solutions while working closely with teammates across disciplines. I am confident my technical skills, positive mindset, and willingness to learn would make me a valuable addition to your organization.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome an opportunity to discuss how my background and enthusiasm can support your team\\u2019s goals.\\n\\nSincerely,  \\n[Your Name]\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2716"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:a80520884fa7d49dfe5d11e34fc6b0fbf461ca935f256cc9f23adada7e955723", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3109", "family": "ifeval-source-3109", "sample_id": "sha256:2630f539544b73d108e1e98e044eeb2bd07bdfa474d7f839cc583e91c6558366", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a short fiction about adulthood. Make sure the word cousins appears more than 2 times.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"At thirty-two, Maya learned adulthood was mostly remembering passwords, watering plants, and pretending she understood insurance.\\n\\nOn Sundays, she visited her grandmother with her cousins. The cousins argued over old photographs, laughed at childhood disasters, and complained about work. For a few hours, adulthood loosened its grip.\\n\\nOne evening, Maya\\u2019s grandmother handed her a recipe stained with flour. \\u201cYou\\u2019re in charge now,\\u201d she said.\\n\\nMaya looked at her cousins. They looked back, equally terrified.\\n\\nThen they began cooking together. The cousins burned the first batch, ruined the second, and finally made something delicious.\\n\\nMaya realized adulthood wasn\\u2019t knowing what to do. It was showing up with your cousins, making mistakes, and staying for dinner.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-202/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3109"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": []}

